mmc: sunxi: power up hosts with a power sequence from the rescan work

The H700 handhelds' SDIO Wi-Fi power sequence waits 200 ms after reset.
mmc_start_host() runs it inside probe, and root mounting waits for all
probes, so it delayed every boot by ~0.1 s after the root card was ready.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -1464,6 +1464,14 @@
 
 	/* TODO: This driver doesn't support HS400 mode yet */
 	mmc->caps2 &= ~MMC_CAP2_HS400;
+
+	/*
+	 * A power sequence (SDIO Wi-Fi) can sleep for hundreds of
+	 * milliseconds. Power up from the rescan work rather than probe:
+	 * the kernel waits for every probe before mounting root.
+	 */
+	if (mmc->pwrseq)
+		mmc->caps2 |= MMC_CAP2_NO_PRESCAN_POWERUP;
 
 	ret = sunxi_mmc_init_host(host);
 	if (ret)
